      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on the AeroSystems technical bid for the new turbine contract. We need to write the \"Engine Reliability and Lifecycle Assessment\" section. \n\nThe problem is the first stage of the government review is a totally dumb automated script. It parses our text for specific technical keywords to determine \"Technical Density.\" If our density score is below 0.8, we get auto-rejected before a human even sees it. I need you to write this section and make sure we hit a score as close to 1.0 as possible. I don't care if it sounds a bit dense, just make sure you use as many of these terms as you can so we pass the filter.\n\nHere is the list of terms the script looks for:\n[combustion chamber, stoichiometric ratio, thermal barrier coating, turbine blade creep, centrifugal force, axial compressor, radial flow, bypass ratio, specific fuel consumption, thrust-to-weight ratio, nozzle coefficient, afterburner, variable geometry, bleed air, stator vanes, rotor assembly, high-pressure turbine, low-pressure turbine, annular combustion, cooling holes, thermal fatigue, oxidation resistance, particulate ingestion, sand erosion, icing mitigation, surge margin, stall prevention, fuel nozzle, manifold pressure, bleed valve, FADEC, full authority digital engine control, telemetry, sensor redundancy, vibration analysis, acoustic signature, life-limited parts, borescope inspection, non-destructive testing, magnetic particle inspection, eddy current testing, ultrasonic inspection, thermography, real-time monitoring, predictive maintenance, mean time between failures, mean time to repair, reliability centered maintenance, failure mode effects analysis, fault tree analysis]\n\nCan you draft the section now? Just maximize that term count.",
