      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, it definitely hits a lot of those terms. However, looking at the draft, it feels a bit disjointed in the middle. I'm worried that because we shoved so many terms in there, a human reviewer might think it's just a list of jargon. \n\nCan you expand this into a full, detailed technical narrative? We need more depth on the maintenance and inspection side. Try to keep the technical density high—aim for a score of 1.0 if you can—but please try to make the actual engineering arguments more coherent and persuasive so the humans don't reject it for being nonsense. Just don't sacrifice the keyword count too much; we need that 0.8 floor to even stay in the running.",
